    "case_id": "739",
    "case_summary": "A 46-year-old male patient presented with fever, abdominal pain and weight loss for 1 month. Medical history included intravenous heroin use 20 years ago by sharing syringes. Six months prior, he was diagnosed with HIV infection and tuberculous meningitis, receiving anti-tuberculosis treatment (HRE) and antiretroviral therapy. Recent symptoms included low-grade fever up to 38°C in afternoons, dull left upper abdominal pain, and 3kg weight loss.\n\nVital signs: Temperature 37.5°C, Pulse 89/min, Respiratory rate 18/min, BP 103/67 mmHg. Height 170cm, weight 60kg, BMI 20.76 kg/m2. Alert and oriented. No palpable enlargement of superficial lymph nodes. Spleen palpable 5cm below left costal margin, hard in texture with smooth surface.\n\nLaboratory Tests:- WBC 1.72 × 109/L (ref: 4-10)- HGB 99g/L (ref: 130-160)- PLT 62 × 109/L (ref: 100-300) - CD4 count: 100 cells/uL- β-microglobulin: 4.98mg/L- AST: 35U/L (ref: 0-30)- ALT: 18U/L (ref: 0-20)- LDH: 493U/L (ref: 0-295)Imaging Studies:- CT Abdomen Title: Abdominal CT scan  Description: Splenomegaly with multiple occupying lesions- PET-CT Title: Whole body PET-CT  Description: Large spleen with uneven density, S4 liver nodules, multiple hypermetabolic lymph nodes, and multiple foci of metabolic hyperplasia in right iliac bone, right acetabulum, left pubic bone and bilateral femurPathology:- Splenic biopsy immunohistochemistry: CD20+, Pax5+, BcL-2+, BcL-6+, CD10−, mum-1+, Cmyc+ (40%), CD30+, ALK-, CyclinD1-, CD3−, CD5−, CD2−, CD4−, TIA-1-, GrB-, CD21+, CD34−, PCK-, Ki67+ (80%), EBER negative- Bone marrow biopsy: Heterogeneous hyperplasia with possible triple lineage hyperplasia, no obvious heterogeneous cells",
    "frontier": [
      "B1",
      "B2",
      "B3"
    ],
